<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.4.2: Defining Functions by a Rule</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00900</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.4.2: Defining Functions by a Rule</md:title>
    <md:uuid>15cb9660-9d51-480c-ac9c-cb8db8e8ca5a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>For 1 - 4, match each equation with a verbal description that represents the same function. </para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="32e60369-cf54-4d64-98aa-ddb3caaf2b97"><problem><para>
      <para>\(f(x)=3x−7\)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3.</para><para>Subtract 7 from the input, then multiply the result by 3.</para><para>Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.</para><para>Divide the input by 3, and then subtract 7 from the result.</para></problem><solution><para>Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.</para><para>
      <para>Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--END QUESTION.-->
  
  
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q1d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3afd615d-65d5-4183-9c36-f828395b7160" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3." data-solution-options="[&quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Subtract 7 from the input, then multiply the result by 3.&quot;, &quot;Multiply the input by 3, then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;, &quot;Divide the input by 3, and then subtract 7 from the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(h(x)\;=\;\frac{x-7}{3}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Subtract 7 from the input, then divide the result by 3.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  
  <section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="d4ff6a33-3678-47ae-8089-254e858309ff"><problem><para>
        <para>For one of the functions, when the input is 6, the output is –3. Which is that function: \(f\), \(g\), \(h\), or \(k\)? </para>
        </para></problem><solution><para>\(g\)</para><para>
        <para> Try Again.</para>
      </para></solution></exercise></section><solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->


<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain how you knew the answer to question 5.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers: Your answers may vary. </para>
    <para>The correct answer is \(k(x)\). When x is 0, \(k(x)\) has the greatest value because \(k(0) = \frac{0 - 7}{3} = - \frac{7}{3} = -2 \frac13\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="834a1a5b-36c8-4d51-889f-2ed2f0303ef2"><problem><para>
      <para>Which function value, \(f\), \(g\), \(h\), or \(k\) is the greatest when the input is 0.</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>\(k\)</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! When \(x\) is 0, \(k(x)\) has the greatest value.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--Interaction End -->


